\section{Introduction}
Alutor (ISO 639-3 \texttt{alr}) is a Chukotko-Kamchatkan language of the eastern Kamchatka Peninsula (Koryak district), Russia, spoken mainly by the elderly. Search results show only academic documentation; no school material was found. The contents of the pages below were not opened, only seen in search results.

\section{Primary Educational Resources}
None found.

\section{Linguistic and Reference Materials}
\begin{itemize}
\item Glottolog reference record for Kibrik, Kodzasov and Muravyova (2004), Alutor grammar in \emph{Language and folklore of the Alutor people} (ed.\ M.\ Kurebito, ELPR, Osaka): \url{https://glottolog.org/resource/reference/id/310908}
\item Second Glottolog record for the same authors (listed with grammar sketch, text and dictionary): \url{https://glottolog.org/resource/reference/id/549951}
\item Nagayama, Nutayulgin and Chechulina, Nymylan--Russian dictionary of the Alutor dialect (Sapporo, 2017 and 2019, two parts) and Nagayama (2015) \emph{Materials on the language of the Nymylan-Alutors}: seen in search results as bibliographic entries; no direct URL to them was found. A paper by Nagayama in a Kushiro repository (Japanese): \url{https://kushiro.repo.nii.ac.jp/record/2000034/files/人文･自然科学_永山ゆかり.pdf}
\end{itemize}

\section{Religious and Community Resources}
No scripture or community organisation was found.

\section{Digital and Audio Resources}
Overview pages on the Alutor people and language (content not examined):
\begin{itemize}
\item \url{https://lingsib.iea.ras.ru/en/languages/aliutor.shtml}
\item \url{https://atlaskmns.ru/page/en/lang_alutorcy_all.html}
\end{itemize}
No audio or video corpus was found.

\section{Curriculum Development Context}
Alutor is not known to be taught in schools, and with about 99 speakers, mostly elderly, any curriculum would depend on the Kibrik grammar and Nagayama dictionaries and on urgent documentation work with remaining speakers. Moll's 1960 Koryak--Russian dictionary concerns the related Koryak language and is not an Alutor resource.

\end{document}
